Third-party components in the Vornik agent image, and where their source is
===========================================================================

This image contains programs that are not part of Vornik and are not covered
by Vornik's licence. Each keeps its own licence; the texts and copyright
notices are in the directories beside this file (/usr/share/licenses/).
Vornik's own programs only run them as separate programs.

1. The piper text-to-speech bundle, in /opt/piper
-------------------------------------------------

Release bundle: rhasspy/piper release 2023.11.14-2
  https://github.com/rhasspy/piper/releases/tag/2023.11.14-2
  piper_linux_x86_64.tar.gz  sha256 a50cb45f355b7af1f6d758c1b360717877ba0a398cc8cbe6d2a7a3a26e225992
  piper_linux_aarch64.tar.gz sha256 fea0fd2d87c54dbc7078d0f878289f404bd4d6eea6e7444a77835d1537ab88eb
The bundle is installed unmodified.

It contains espeak-ng, licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later (licenses/espeak-ng/),
dynamically linked with piper and piper-phonemize (MIT) and onnxruntime (MIT).

The source code it was built from:

  component        repository                 ref                commit
  espeak-ng        rhasspy/espeak-ng          master (note)      0f65aa301e0d6bae5e172cc74197d32a6182200f
  piper            rhasspy/piper              2023.11.14-2       38917ffd8c0e219c6581d73e07b30ef1d572fce1
  piper-phonemize  rhasspy/piper-phonemize    2023.11.14-4       fccd4f335aa68ac0b72600822f34d84363daa2bf
  onnxruntime      microsoft/onnxruntime      v1.14.1            c57cf374b67f72575546d7b4c69a1af4972e2b54
  spdlog           gabime/spdlog              v1.12.0            7e635fca68d014934b4af8a1cf874f63989352b7
  fmt              fmtlib/fmt                 10.0.0             a0b8a92e3d1532361c2f7feb63babc5c18d00ef2

piper's build fetched piper-phonemize and espeak-ng from their default
branches rather than from pinned commits. The two commits above are the
branch heads at the time the 2023.11.14-2 release was built (2023-11-14; the
espeak-ng commit itself is dated 2023-09-13), established from
the repositories' history and checked against the bundle's own espeak-ng data
files. The fmt 9.1.0 compiled into piper is the copy bundled inside spdlog
(include/spdlog/fmt/bundled); fmt 10.0.0 is listed because piper's build
fetches it. onnxruntime is listed at its tag's own tree; its git submodules
(cmake/external) are not included and are named, at their pinned commits, by
that tree's .gitmodules and cmake/deps.txt.

Where to get it. Each repository above is public at
https://github.com/<repository>/tree/<commit>. The same sources, as the
unmodified GitHub archives of those commits with their sha256 checksums, are
attached, free of charge, to every Vornik Community Edition release at
https://github.com/EaseIT-cz/vornik/releases as

  vornik-agent-third-party-source-piper-2023.11.14-2.tar

One archive serves both architectures. It is produced by
scripts/third-party-source-archive.sh in the Vornik Community Edition source
(https://github.com/EaseIT-cz/vornik), which refuses an archive whose
checksum differs.

Earlier images. The archive is attached to release 2026.10.6 and later. It
is also the corresponding source for the agent images distributed before it
with the same bundle: releases 2026.9.7, 2026.9.8, 2026.10.1, 2026.10.2,
2026.10.3, 2026.10.4 and 2026.10.5, and every agent image built from the
main branch since 2026-09-26, when the bundle entered the image. All of them
carry piper release 2023.11.14-2, the only release the image has used, so the
archive above is their source too.

Licences besides GPL-3.0-or-later and MIT. espeak-ng's getopt compatibility
code is BSD-2-Clause (espeak-ng/COPYING.BSD2); espeak-ng/COPYING.APACHE and
espeak-ng/COPYING.UCD are the upstream repository's other licence files.
onnxruntime incorporates third-party components under their own licences,
listed in onnxruntime/ThirdPartyNotices.txt. uni-algo, compiled into
piper-phonemize, is public domain or MIT (piper-phonemize/uni-algo-LICENSE.md).

2. whisper.cpp, in /usr/local/bin/whisper-cli
---------------------------------------------

Built from https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp at commit
48f628a84833905ee4a0658ee6d4a5c915ce1997 (v1.8.7). MIT licence
(licenses/whisper.cpp/).

3. Everything else
------------------

The operating system packages come from Ubuntu 24.04; their copyright files
are in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright and their source is in the Ubuntu
archive (apt-get source <package>). The Go toolchain in /usr/local/go carries
its own LICENSE.
